# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# COOP + COEP turn on SharedArrayBuffer, which lets the OxiPNG and AVIF encoders
# use their multi-threaded builds instead of falling back to a single core.
# Safe here because Pare loads nothing cross-origin - there is no server, no CDN
# script and no third-party asset to be blocked.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy (ADR-040) allows only this site's own files.
# Each exception has one reason:
#   'wasm-unsafe-eval'  the codecs are WebAssembly
#   sha256-...          the theme script inlined in index.html, which must run
#                       before first paint (tests/unit/csp.test.ts keeps the
#                       hash in step with the script)
#   blob: and data:     dropped files, and the copies of a site the checker
#                       renders - those pages inherit this policy, so their
#                       inline styles need 'unsafe-inline' too
# The production tests run under exactly this file: vite.config.ts reads it.
#
# Scripts under /assets/ get their own policy below, and that is the one a
# worker runs under - workers take the policy of their own script, not the
# page's. It adds one thing: 'unsafe-eval', because the WOFF2 codec's
# Emscripten glue writes small functions with `new Function` as it loads. No
# page code runs under it, and nothing a user drops is ever run as script.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'sha256-nRmOin9fjJbu2X5d0A9lIhXl6y9TNtoq6gxrKV8j9FU='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' blob: data:; img-src 'self' blob: data:; font-src 'self' blob: data:; connect-src 'self' blob: data:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' blob:; media-src 'self' blob: data:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'

# The service worker must never be served stale, or a deploy never takes over.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Everything under /assets/ has a content hash in its name, so it can never
# change under the same URL. Cache it for a year: a returning visitor then never
# re-downloads the encoders (several MB each), and the CDN serves them from the
# edge. This is most of what "scaling" means for a site with no server.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' blob: data:; img-src 'self' blob: data:; font-src 'self' blob: data:; connect-src 'self' blob: data:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' blob:; media-src 'self' blob: data:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'
